// Prototype for Phase 12 / M12.3: can a real evermore-agentd recipe be
// authored as nscript source instead of hand-written TOML?
//
// This mirrors the read-only slice of the built-in `packages.doctor` recipe
// (crates/evermore-agentd/recipes/packages.doctor.toml): one catalogue read
// (`packages.list_installed`) and a rendered report. It deliberately leaves
// out `packages.doctor`'s `choose` step (publisher/name form input) and its
// second read (`packages.explain_dependencies`, which needs that input) --
// nscript has no native primitive for "a typed value the host's own UI
// collects before the program runs" (its `key = host("label")` mechanism is
// typed for opaque signing-key material, not a reusable form-input slot),
// so that half of `packages.doctor` has no faithful nscript translation yet.
// See ../README.md for what this does and does not prove.
use evermore_packages

permissions {
    packages_read
    log
}

let installed = evermore_packages.list_installed()?
print("Installed packages: " + text(installed.count))
